1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,416
Welcome to ADVISIO.

2
00:00:01,846 --> 00:00:05,004
This walkthrough follows the Research
Coordinator's tools, from

3
00:00:05,062 --> 00:00:08,754
workflow planning and researcher
participation to academic records

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,170
and defense results.

5
00:00:10,767 --> 00:00:13,112
Sign in with your authorized
coordinator account.

6
00:00:13,704 --> 00:00:16,793
The Research Coordinator uses the
Course Professor workspace,

7
00:00:17,106 --> 00:00:19,370
identified by the Coordinator Portal
badge.

8
00:00:19,962 --> 00:00:23,108
This demonstration uses fictional
accounts and research records

9
00:00:23,155 --> 00:00:25,442
within an isolated local workspace.

10
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:29,760
Overview summarizes the research
groups, submissions, and activities

11
00:00:29,806 --> 00:00:30,468
you monitor.

12
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:35,356
The sidebar connects Workflow,
Research Projects, Submissions, Class

13
00:00:35,425 --> 00:00:37,736
Record, Progress, and Defense.

14
00:00:38,421 --> 00:00:40,673
These areas have distinct
responsibilities.

15
00:00:41,172 --> 00:00:43,041
Enrollment controls participation;

16
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:45,317
a registered project tracks the study;

17
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:48,359
and academic decisions are recorded
against the applicable

18
00:00:48,393 --> 00:00:50,367
submission or defense cycle.

19
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,742
Open Workflow and choose Create
another workflow.

20
00:00:54,241 --> 00:00:57,538
Enter a descriptive name and select
the research type available

21
00:00:57,573 --> 00:00:59,036
within your assigned program.

22
00:00:59,628 --> 00:01:01,323
Save the workflow as a draft.

23
00:01:01,753 --> 00:01:03,819
A draft is a private configuration:

24
00:01:04,249 --> 00:01:07,848
saving it does not publish milestones
or enroll researchers.

25
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:11,772
We will continue with a prepared draft
to examine its structure.

26
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:14,677
Topics organize related milestones.

27
00:01:15,177 --> 00:01:18,776
Milestones define the research steps,
and document milestones

28
00:01:18,822 --> 00:01:20,448
contain submission requirements.

29
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:24,499
Our prepared example begins with
Adviser Selection, then Title

30
00:01:24,523 --> 00:01:28,377
Proposal, a proposal manuscript, and
Defense Eligibility.

31
00:01:28,969 --> 00:01:31,907
This sequence is an example configured
for the tutorial;

32
00:01:32,406 --> 00:01:34,310
departments can choose a different
order.

33
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:38,757
Inspect a milestone's instructions,
submission mode, required files,

34
00:01:38,791 --> 00:01:39,964
and approval settings.

35
00:01:40,463 --> 00:01:44,294
A relative target, such as fourteen
days, differs from a calendar

36
00:01:44,353 --> 00:01:45,119
target date.

37
00:01:45,711 --> 00:01:49,333
Required Milestone Condition
identifies an earlier prerequisite.

38
00:01:50,018 --> 00:01:53,431
Defense Eligibility is an academic
event type that provides an

39
00:01:53,466 --> 00:01:56,903
explicit coordinator approval gate for
a later defense cycle.

40
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,704
Guides and Templates stores supporting
resources for the workflow.

41
00:02:01,134 --> 00:02:04,791
Choose Upload resource, enter its
title and description, and attach

42
00:02:04,838 --> 00:02:06,033
the demonstration guide.

43
00:02:06,463 --> 00:02:09,331
Save the resource and confirm that it
appears in the list.

44
00:02:09,923 --> 00:02:12,709
These reference materials support the
configured requirements;

45
00:02:13,301 --> 00:02:16,354
uploading a guide does not count as a
researcher's submission.

46
00:02:16,967 --> 00:02:19,742
Return to the workflow structure and
review its summary.

47
00:02:20,171 --> 00:02:24,142
Topics, milestone assignments, and
required submissions must be

48
00:02:24,188 --> 00:02:25,907
configured before publication.

49
00:02:26,406 --> 00:02:30,353
Select Publish, inspect the readiness
information, and confirm when

50
00:02:30,388 --> 00:02:31,526
the workflow is ready.

51
00:02:32,211 --> 00:02:35,300
The published state makes the
configured process available through

52
00:02:35,323 --> 00:02:36,391
its enrollment rules.

53
00:02:37,076 --> 00:02:40,721
Publication does not automatically
approve participation requests or

54
00:02:40,791 --> 00:02:42,927
rewrite existing student submissions.

55
00:02:43,533 --> 00:02:47,538
Participants separates Members, Join
requests, and Invitations.

56
00:02:48,038 --> 00:02:50,220
Generate a workflow code or shared
link.

57
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:54,040
We now switch to a fictional
researcher's account to request access

58
00:02:54,121 --> 00:02:55,189
using that code.

59
00:02:55,782 --> 00:02:58,533
The request is pending until the
coordinator reviews it.

60
00:02:59,126 --> 00:03:02,760
Return to the coordinator account,
open Join requests, and approve

61
00:03:02,794 --> 00:03:03,955
the prepared request.

62
00:03:04,547 --> 00:03:06,521
The researcher then appears in
Members.

63
00:03:06,893 --> 00:03:10,202
Direct invitations are a separate
option for registered researchers,

64
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:13,603
and the recipient must accept before
enrollment becomes active.

65
00:03:14,195 --> 00:03:17,667
Joining a workflow and registering a
research title remain separate

66
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:18,410
steps.

67
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:22,319
This prepared, enrolled group is at
Adviser Selection.

68
00:03:22,818 --> 00:03:26,591
In the group leader's account, open
the milestone and send a request

69
00:03:26,626 --> 00:03:28,019
to an eligible adviser.

70
00:03:28,518 --> 00:03:30,121
The request remains pending.

71
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:34,219
We switch to the adviser's own account
to review and accept it, then

72
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,077
return to coordinator monitoring.

73
00:03:36,762 --> 00:03:40,152
The accepted assignment updates the
recorded milestone progress.

74
00:03:40,651 --> 00:03:42,729
The coordinator monitors this process;

75
00:03:43,159 --> 00:03:46,758
the coordinator account is not used to
make the adviser's decision.

76
00:03:47,367 --> 00:03:50,954
At Title Proposal, the group leader
submits the required proposed

77
00:03:50,989 --> 00:03:51,593
titles.

78
00:03:51,965 --> 00:03:55,111
Switch back to the coordinator account
and open the title review.

79
00:03:55,703 --> 00:03:58,861
Read the alternatives and use feedback
when a revision is needed.

80
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:03,157
For the prepared acceptable proposal,
select a title and approve it.

81
00:04:03,749 --> 00:04:06,930
The approved title registers the
research project while preserving

82
00:04:06,988 --> 00:04:10,715
the existing group's workflow,
members, adviser assignment, and

83
00:04:10,785 --> 00:04:11,911
recorded progress.

84
00:04:12,596 --> 00:04:16,009
Approval is an academic review
decision, rather than a routine

85
00:04:16,044 --> 00:04:17,507
registration shortcut.

86
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:21,281
Research Projects lists registered
studies within the workflows you

87
00:04:21,339 --> 00:04:21,989
oversee.

88
00:04:22,581 --> 00:04:26,146
Locate the approved demonstration
title and inspect its project and

89
00:04:26,227 --> 00:04:27,342
workflow information.

90
00:04:28,027 --> 00:04:31,103
Open Progress to compare the current
milestones and recorded

91
00:04:31,149 --> 00:04:32,148
completion states.

92
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:35,782
Pending requirements indicate where
further work or guidance is

93
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:36,269
needed.

94
00:04:36,862 --> 00:04:39,950
The configured conditions still
determine which milestone the group

95
00:04:40,008 --> 00:04:41,227
can start next.

96
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:43,934
Open Submissions and its Review Queue.

97
00:04:44,527 --> 00:04:47,975
The workspace shows the exact
submitted document beside comments and

98
00:04:48,044 --> 00:04:48,973
review controls.

99
00:04:49,403 --> 00:04:53,466
Select a passage in this text-based
PDF, attach a comment, and post

100
00:04:53,513 --> 00:04:53,768
it.

101
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,878
A posted comment is saved
independently of an academic decision.

102
00:04:58,563 --> 00:05:01,558
Enter decision feedback and request
revision when the submission

103
00:05:01,604 --> 00:05:02,823
needs further work.

104
00:05:03,433 --> 00:05:05,859
Here is a separate prepared revised
submission.

105
00:05:06,289 --> 00:05:09,331
Inspect its submitted version and
earlier attempt history.

106
00:05:09,923 --> 00:05:13,580
Adviser and other mandatory reviewer
approvals apply to the exact

107
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:14,892
version being reviewed.

108
00:05:15,391 --> 00:05:18,689
Once those checks are satisfied and
the work meets the requirement,

109
00:05:18,898 --> 00:05:20,929
the coordinator can approve the
submission.

110
00:05:21,522 --> 00:05:23,983
Any grade is recorded and released
separately;

111
00:05:24,354 --> 00:05:27,954
an approval decision does not itself
publish a score.

112
00:05:28,567 --> 00:05:31,609
Class Record uses the active
researcher roster of an owned

113
00:05:31,655 --> 00:05:32,340
workflow.

114
00:05:32,712 --> 00:05:35,463
The periods are Prelim, Midterm, and
Finals.

115
00:05:36,055 --> 00:05:39,701
Individual activities, eligible linked
milestone scores, and

116
00:05:39,759 --> 00:05:42,058
attendance support the recorded
calculations.

117
00:05:42,650 --> 00:05:46,051
Review the prepared activity scores
and attendance marks, make the

118
00:05:46,086 --> 00:05:49,186
demonstration correction, and save the
private drafts.

119
00:05:49,778 --> 00:05:51,566
Saving does not release grades.

120
00:05:51,996 --> 00:05:55,583
When required entries and calculations
are complete, Release period

121
00:05:55,653 --> 00:05:57,987
publishes a snapshot for the active
roster.

122
00:05:58,579 --> 00:06:01,389
The researcher's My Grades view then
shows that researcher's

123
00:06:01,447 --> 00:06:02,306
released result.

124
00:06:02,898 --> 00:06:06,242
Later draft edits remain private, and
corrections create a new

125
00:06:06,311 --> 00:06:09,713
recorded release rather than rewriting
the earlier snapshot.

126
00:06:10,333 --> 00:06:13,712
Defense preparation begins with the
configured Defense Eligibility

127
00:06:13,781 --> 00:06:14,489
milestone.

128
00:06:14,989 --> 00:06:17,891
Review the group's prerequisites and
required submissions.

129
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:21,165
This prepared group is ready for
coordinator approval.

130
00:06:21,595 --> 00:06:24,811
Approve its eligibility and inspect
the updated status.

131
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,375
The approval belongs to this group and
milestone for one defense

132
00:06:28,398 --> 00:06:28,979
cycle.

133
00:06:29,408 --> 00:06:32,798
Adviser acceptance or completion of
unrelated workflow activities

134
00:06:33,007 --> 00:06:35,364
does not replace this explicit
approval.

135
00:06:35,967 --> 00:06:39,032
Request the Dean signature for a group
with approved, unused

136
00:06:39,090 --> 00:06:39,949
eligibility.

137
00:06:40,448 --> 00:06:43,920
Select the authorized dean, review the
subject and message, and

138
00:06:43,978 --> 00:06:45,835
attach the prepared PDF letter.

139
00:06:46,428 --> 00:06:50,143
Send the request and keep its pending
status distinct from approval.

140
00:06:50,735 --> 00:06:53,707
We then switch to the dean's own
account, where the request is

141
00:06:53,777 --> 00:06:54,833
reviewed and signed.

142
00:06:55,426 --> 00:06:58,328
Scheduling requires that valid signed
letter to be linked to this

143
00:06:58,374 --> 00:06:59,837
same eligibility cycle;

144
00:07:00,209 --> 00:07:03,367
an earlier defense letter cannot
unlock a later cycle.

145
00:07:03,967 --> 00:07:07,299
This separate prepared group already
has approved eligibility and

146
00:07:07,357 --> 00:07:09,029
its corresponding signed letter.

147
00:07:09,528 --> 00:07:13,023
Create a defense event, select the
eligible group, and enter the

148
00:07:13,069 --> 00:07:15,519
schedule, venue, and session details.

149
00:07:16,204 --> 00:07:19,872
Assign a panel chair and the required
panelist, then choose Create

150
00:07:19,907 --> 00:07:21,149
Event and Invite.

151
00:07:21,834 --> 00:07:23,471
Invitations begin pending.

152
00:07:23,971 --> 00:07:26,920
We inspect the responses through the
participants' own accounts

153
00:07:26,978 --> 00:07:28,893
before continuing with preparation.

154
00:07:29,578 --> 00:07:33,177
Creating an event does not mean every
participant has accepted.

155
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,681
Open the session's defense documents.

156
00:07:36,052 --> 00:07:39,419
Select the approved, immutable
manuscript submitted for its Defense

157
00:07:39,477 --> 00:07:40,870
Eligibility milestone.

158
00:07:41,463 --> 00:07:44,771
Configure the structured form and
inspect the researcher roster,

159
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:48,684
rating levels, individual presentation
criteria, and group

160
00:07:48,754 --> 00:07:50,066
manuscript criteria.

161
00:07:50,751 --> 00:07:53,491
Review the scoring weights and
publication requirements.

162
00:07:54,176 --> 00:07:57,659
Once the required participants and
materials are ready, publish the

163
00:07:57,705 --> 00:07:58,204
packet.

164
00:07:58,889 --> 00:08:02,047
Publication preserves the selected
manuscript and evaluation

165
00:08:02,105 --> 00:08:04,230
configuration for authorized
panelists;

166
00:08:04,822 --> 00:08:08,537
it does not submit their evaluations
or release an official result.

167
00:08:09,133 --> 00:08:12,395
When the session conditions are
satisfied, the coordinator can start

168
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:13,429
the live defense.

169
00:08:14,021 --> 00:08:16,761
We then open an accepted panelist's
own workspace.

170
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:20,987
The panelist reviews the prepared
ratings, previews the evaluation,

171
00:08:21,161 --> 00:08:23,761
confirms it, and submits the final
record.

172
00:08:24,446 --> 00:08:27,000
Panelists make these decisions through
their own accounts.

173
00:08:27,593 --> 00:08:31,087
The coordinator cannot complete a
missing panelist evaluation by

174
00:08:31,145 --> 00:08:32,864
selecting an official outcome.

175
00:08:33,467 --> 00:08:37,252
We now use a separate prepared session
with all required evaluations

176
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:38,065
finalized.

177
00:08:38,657 --> 00:08:42,000
Inspect the consolidated individual
and manuscript results and

178
00:08:42,070 --> 00:08:44,276
verify the recorded evaluation
history.

179
00:08:44,961 --> 00:08:48,328
Select the official decision
separately from the calculated scores.

180
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:52,391
Enter revision instructions when
required, then confirm and release

181
00:08:52,426 --> 00:08:53,065
the result.

182
00:08:53,750 --> 00:08:56,304
The released outcome controls the
group's next steps.

183
00:08:56,896 --> 00:08:59,775
A passed defense consumes that cycle's
eligibility;

184
00:09:00,274 --> 00:09:03,653
revisions or another defense follow
their recorded requirements.

185
00:09:04,267 --> 00:09:07,425
Announcements sends an update to
active participants in the selected

186
00:09:07,471 --> 00:09:08,133
workflow.

187
00:09:08,632 --> 00:09:12,220
Choose the workflow, review the
demonstration message and audience,

188
00:09:12,336 --> 00:09:13,183
and publish it.

189
00:09:13,868 --> 00:09:17,607
Messages supports group collaboration,
while Inbox handles formal

190
00:09:17,653 --> 00:09:18,547
correspondence.

191
00:09:19,046 --> 00:09:23,261
Calendar, Manuscript Reviews, and
Official Copies provide related

192
00:09:23,331 --> 00:09:25,211
records under your account's
permissions.

193
00:09:25,803 --> 00:09:29,182
Return to Progress to monitor the
researchers' next steps after each

194
00:09:29,228 --> 00:09:30,041
decision.

195
00:09:30,633 --> 00:09:33,756
That concludes the ADVISIO Research
Coordinator walkthrough.

196
00:09:34,348 --> 00:09:38,017
The example connects workflow
planning, participation, research

197
00:09:38,063 --> 00:09:41,361
review, academic records, and defense
coordination.

198
00:09:41,953 --> 00:09:44,577
Return to any chapter when you need to
review a specific

199
00:09:44,635 --> 00:09:45,772
responsibility.
